% =========================================================================
% README — Quadrotor 3D Simulation: Modular Structure
% =========================================================================
%
% HOW TO RUN
% ----------
% 1. Place all .m files in the same folder (or add to MATLAB path)
% 2. Open and run: main.m
%    >> run('main.m')
%
% FILE STRUCTURE
% --------------
%
%   main.m                   ← Entry point. Run this. Contains:
%                                - calls get_params + get_trajectory
%                                - initial conditions
%                                - ode45 call
%                                - post-processing call
%                                - metrics & plots call
%
%   get_params.m             ← Physical parameters + fault settings
%                               Edit here to change mass, inertia, limits, fault
%
%   get_trajectory.m         ← Reference trajectory (position + derivatives)
%                               Edit here to change trajectory shape
%                               Takes params as input, returns params with
%                               trajectory fields appended
%
%   pid_controller.m         ← PID controller (all gains defined here)
%                               Returns struct u with u1/u2/u3/u4
%
%   control_allocation.m     ← Maps [u1,u2,u3,u4] → [T1,T2,T3,T4]
%                               Handles rotor failure + saturation
%
%   get_alpha.m              ← Fault logic (effectiveness of T1)
%                               Called by both dynamics AND reconstruct
%
%   quadrotor3D_dynamics.m   ← ODE right-hand-side for ode45
%                               Calls: pid_controller, control_allocation
%
%   reconstruct_signals.m    ← Post-simulation signal logging
%                               Calls the SAME: pid_controller, control_allocation
%                               No duplicated code — always in sync
%
%   plot_results.m           ← All figures in one place
%
%   performance_metrics.m    ← Prints RMS, IAE, ISE, ITAE, steady-state
%
%   quadrotor3D_animate.m    ← 3D animation (uncomment in main.m to use)
%
%
% HOW TO CHANGE THINGS
% --------------------
%
%   Change physical parameters (mass, inertia, arm length, etc.):
%     → Edit get_params.m
%     → Automatically picked up by everything via the params struct
%
%   Change fault settings:
%     → Edit get_params.m:
%         params.fault_enable = 1;
%         params.fault_mode   = 2;     % inject during flight
%         params.fault_time   = 10;    % seconds
%         params.alpha_T1     = 0;     % 0=fully failed, 0.5=partial
%
%   Change reference trajectory:
%     → Edit get_trajectory.m
%     → Update x_des, y_des, z_des AND all their derivatives
%       (velocity and acceleration) to stay consistent
%
%   Change PID gains:
%     → Edit pid_controller.m (gains section)
%     → Automatically applies to both simulation and post-processing
%
%   Switch to a different controller (LQR, SMC, MPC, etc.):
%     1. Create new_controller.m with IDENTICAL signature:
%            function u = new_controller(t, x, p)
%            % Returns u.u1, u.u2, u.u3, u.u4, u.phi_des, u.theta_des, u.psi_des
%     2. In main.m, change ONE line:
%            [t, x] = ode45(@(t,x) quadrotor3D_dynamics(t, x, params, @new_controller), ...
%     3. Also update the reconstruct_signals call:
%            logs = reconstruct_signals(t, x, params, @new_controller);
%     → Nothing else changes
%
%   Add new plots:
%     → Edit plot_results.m (all logs are available in the logs struct)

% =====================================================================
    % FAULT SETTINGS
    % =====================================================================
    % HOW TO USE:
    %
    %   HEALTHY MODE (no fault):
    %       fault_enable = 0
    %       (all other fault params below are completely IGNORED)
    %
    %   FAULT MODE — pre-existing (active from t = 0):
    %       fault_enable = 1
    %       fault_mode   = 1
    %       alpha_T1     = 0      (or any value in 0..1)
    %
    %   FAULT MODE — injected mid-flight:
    %       fault_enable = 1
    %       fault_mode   = 2
    %       fault_time   = 10     (seconds — must be > 0)
    %       alpha_T1     = 0      (or any value in 0..1)
    %
    % WARNING: Do NOT set fault_time = 0 with fault_mode = 2.
    %          The condition (t >= fault_time) is always true from t=0,
    %          making it identical to mode 1. Use fault_mode = 1 instead.
    % =====================================================================